      "value": "q0_pay_when_roi_clear",
      "rationale": "As a busy parent juggling multiple responsibilities, I'd want to see real value before committing financially. The free tier lets me test whether FocusLoop actually reduces my stress and coordination overhead before paying.",
      "confidence": 0.88
    },
    {
      "questionId": "q1",
      "value": "q1_plus_after_sustained_use",
      "rationale": "Email parsing and grocery list sharing sound useful, but I need to confirm the core calendar and handoff features work well for my family first. Once I've used Plus for a month or two and see clear ROI, I'd consider Pro.",
      "confidence": 0.82
    },
    {
      "questionId": "q2",
      "value": "q2_monthly_cancel_anytime",
      "rationale": "I prefer flexibility. With a young family, priorities shift quickly—school changes, schedules evolve. Monthly billing lets me cancel without penalty if the app stops fitting our needs.",
      "confidence": 0.85
    },
    {
      "questionId": "q3",
      "value": "q3_one_dollar_try_cancel",
      "rationale": "A $1 trial is low-friction enough to test Plus features like email parsing and the digest. I'd try it, but I'd cancel immediately if I don't see clear value beyond what free offers.",
      "confidence": 0.86
    },
    {
      "questionId": "q4",
      "value": "q4_compare_pay_if_wins",
      "rationale": "I'm not against paying for good apps, but I won't switch without comparing. If a friend recommends something, I'd look at both free and paid options and pick the one that genuinely solves our coordination problem better.",
      "confidence": 0.84
    },
    {
      "questionId": "q5",
      "value": "q5_ads_pay_if_plus_useful",
      "rationale": "Ads in a family app would be mildly annoying, but I wouldn't pay just to remove them. I'd only upgrade to Plus if the actual features—digest, handoffs, email parsing—justify the cost. Ad-free is a bonus, not the main reason.",
      "confidence": 0.83
    },
    {
      "questionId": "q6",
      "value": "q6_fair_if_use_justifies",
      "rationale": "Six to twelve dollars monthly isn't outrageous for a tool that could save me hours of coordination stress, but only if I use it daily. If it becomes a routine part of how my family stays organized, the price feels reasonable.",
      "confidence": 0.85
    },
    {
      "questionId": "overall_interest",
      "value": 4,
      "rationale": "FocusLoop directly addresses my biggest pain point—scattered communication across WeChat, email, and paper. The color-coded calendar and task handoffs appeal to me. I'm not at 5 because I need to see it in action first.",
      "confidence": 0.87
    },
